  "id": "COMPOUND:32249 - PROTEIN:4915",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Isoamyl isobutyrate and Replicase polyprotein 1ab through a series of molecular targets. The drug Isoamyl isobutyrate is shown to interact with SNU-387, a cell line that is targeted by multiple compounds, including (1S,3R,6S,8R,11S,12S,15R,16R)-15-[(2R)-4-[(2R)-3,3-dimethyloxiran-2-yl]butan-2-yl]-7,7,12,16-tetramethylpentacyclo[9.7.0.01,3.03,8.012,16]octadecan-6-ol and 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One. These compounds are all implicated in targeting Replicase polyprotein 1ab, a key component of the viral replication machinery. The shared target of SNU-387 and the subsequent compounds suggests a possible mechanism of action involving viral replication or related processes. The evidence is supported by a chain of targets, but the exact mechanism by which Isoamyl isobutyrate influences Replicase polyprotein 1ab remains unclear, requiring further investigation into the specific pathways and interactions involved.",
